{
 "summary": "Moves the `PubkeyProvider` interface into `descriptor.h` and adds a public `ParsePubkey()` function to parse and validate standalone descriptor key expressions using P2TR rules. It adds a `GetOriginInfo()` accessor to `PubkeyProvider` for retrieving explicit key origins and fingerprints without re-parsing. It also fixes a bug in `musig()` descriptor parsing to reject unexpected trailing characters.",
 "problem": "Callers such as GUI wallet setup wizards have no way to validate or inspect isolated key expressions without wrapping them into synthetic descriptor strings, because `PubkeyProvider` and key parsing routines were private to `descriptor.cpp`. Additionally, the descriptor parser previously accepted arbitrary trailing characters after `musig(...)` expressions if they did not begin with `/`.",
 "evidence": [
  "PR description notes this is needed for GUI multisig setup to validate input, inspect parsed keys, and apply policy (rejecting private or uncompressed keys) tracking in issue #35645.",
  "Commit 7a81907c34 points out that 'musig() parser split the input at the closing parenthesis without validating the remaining text. This allowed unexpected characters after the expression to be ignored.'"
 ],
 "dependencies": {
  "depends_on": [],
  "enables": [
   "#35645"
  ]
 },
 "scope_notes": "Commit 086b0cd0b0 is mostly a move-only refactor moving `PubkeyProvider` from `descriptor.cpp` to `descriptor.h`.",
 "changed_since_previous": "The approach, commits, and API surface are unchanged from the previous version.",
 "card": "Exposes the internal PubkeyProvider interface in descriptor.h and introduces a public ParsePubkey function to parse standalone key expressions using Taproot key rules. This allows external modules, such as the multisig setup wizard in issue #35645, to inspect key properties, origins, and derivation paths without constructing dummy descriptor strings. The PR also fixes descriptor parsing to reject trailing text after musig expressions.",
